      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T11:02:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to avoid making methods synchronized since holding lock while outgoing binder call can lead to deadlock (TbsGatt\u0027s methods make binder calls to system Bluetooth service).\n\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1raSGHAFQZY8iq7PCHHLNwK8RcmC5_jmpEj4l817SXbA/edit#heading\u003dh.586244sxj4cs\n\nIn order to get both goals (preventing NPE and not changing running thread), the patch set 5 in this CL could be the solution. Could you take a look? This could be a better solution than current patch set.\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/1991492/5",
